{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>ובני רשף</b> — Some say: just as the nature of a bird is to fly, so the nature of man is to toil. Similar is ולחומי רשף, which means hot ones of the bird [i.e., flying creatures]. Some say: the sons of Resheph who are fit for Gehenna are lifted up in this world, and this interpretation is without Resheph — it is merely cold. Some say: בני רשף — they are sparks of fire, and it [the interpretation] is close, because man is accustomed to seeing the sun rising and setting; its rising and setting are only in his eyes, and because the rain comes only at infrequent intervals, and there are times when the rain is withheld in time of need, the children of man cry out to the Creator and He commands the clouds to rain, and this is for them a great sign; therefore after עושה גדולות He mentioned הנותן מטר."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וזה הפירוש בלא רשף רק הוא קר' is difficult; translated hyper-literally. 'רק הוא קר' may mean 'it is merely cold/flat,' i.e., the interpretation is unconvincing, but the syntax is strained and possibly corrupt. Also uncertain whether 'והוא קרוב' at the start of the third opinion means 'and it [the interpretation] is close [to the truth]' or connects to what follows."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:52.874891901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}